# XSUB - Feed submitted lines to a program

```text
XSUB [DU:]
```

## Enable input

Place XSUB in a .SUB procedure before the program that needs responses.
With XSUB.COM and BATCHIO.RSX on the Utilities disk in B0, use B0:XSUB
B0:. The second B0: gives the location of the matching resident module.

## Example procedure

```text
B0:XSUB B0:
ED XDEMO.TXT
IHELLO FROM XSUB^L^Z
E
:TYPE XDEMO.TXT
```

Use a fresh filename. Save these lines as XDEMO.SUB and run SUBMIT
XDEMO. Type the caret sequences literally. [SUBMIT](SUBMIT.HLP) converts
them to control bytes. Each buffered input request takes the next
procedure line. ED's single-character insert mode still reads the
keyboard.
